WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.662
Gate 7 is the test of the whole model, and
it runs before any population cuts over.

2
00:00:05.662 --> 00:00:07.800
The setup takes three steps.

3
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:12.764
Pick a pilot user who sponsors a non-person
identity and has a managed laptop,

4
00:00:12.764 --> 00:00:15.600
because one test then
reaches three tracks.

5
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:19.137
Record the starting state:
groups, unit, persona,

6
00:00:19.137 --> 00:00:23.400
access packages, the device's
groups and the sponsorship.

7
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.072
Then take a baseline
with the validation kit,

8
00:00:26.072 --> 00:00:29.900
running the HR and dynamic-group
checks against an input folder.

9
00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:32.794
Three files matter: the
owned exceptions list,

10
00:00:32.794 --> 00:00:38.125
the HR export of counts per organization
code, and the previous membership snapshot.

11
00:00:38.125 --> 00:00:42.650
Each run writes its own snapshot,
which becomes the next run's input.

12
00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:45.952
Finally, HR records the
move as a personnel action,

13
00:00:45.952 --> 00:00:49.738
a reassignment from the ledger
code to accounts payable.

14
00:00:49.738 --> 00:00:51.310
Nobody opens a ticket.
